00:22:17.800 --> 00:22:19.980
than we would have thought it even a decade ago.

00:22:21.530 --> 00:22:24.750
The estimates are that more than 95% of the biomass

00:22:24.750 --> 00:22:26.570
in the open ocean is microbial.

00:22:27.540 --> 00:22:29.960
The deep subsurface...

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:33.120
The basalts of the crust of the earth are shot through with life.

00:22:34.420 --> 00:22:38.820
Life is in ice, life is in waters of boiling temperatures.

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:45.800
Why does it matter that we are surrounded by these tiny living beings?

00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:53.960
Because it turns out many of them are doing things essential to the survival of life on earth.

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:59.980
The microbial world is paramount in the context of maintaining the...

00:23:00.120 --> 00:23:01.560
The chemistry of the biosphere.

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:06.680
The biosphere is fundamentally chemistry.

00:23:07.330 --> 00:23:10.810
That chemistry is fundamentally driven by microorganisms.

00:23:11.030 --> 00:23:15.620
Why should we care?

00:23:15.990 --> 00:23:17.110
We can't see these things.

00:23:17.830 --> 00:23:21.090
Well, let's do a thought experiment and take these things away.

00:23:21.370 --> 00:23:23.310
Let's take all the bacteria in the world away.

00:23:23.490 --> 00:23:24.310
Do you know what's going to happen?

00:23:25.990 --> 00:23:28.510
All the life that we can see with our naked eyes,

00:23:28.530 --> 00:23:29.850
all that life is going to disappear.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:38.760
short order. The microbial world is the basis upon which our whole ecosphere rests. And without it,

00:23:38.820 --> 00:23:49.730
there is no multicellular light. The humbling thought is that if you do the converse and take

00:23:49.730 --> 00:23:54.110
away all the animals and plants, you will see big adjustments in the bacterial world,

00:23:54.130 --> 00:23:57.380
but it will still be there growing happily along and evolving.

00:24:01.020 --> 00:24:06.700
message of the work of Carl Woese and Norm Pace that microbes play a key role on our planet

00:24:06.700 --> 00:24:15.030
could hardly be clear. What will happen when we can read the entire score, not just of

00:24:15.030 --> 00:24:21.830
microbes, but of human beings? How will that change our understanding of our role on the planet?

00:24:30.760 --> 00:24:35.850
Without microbes, in all their diversity, the entire balance of the planet would be in jeopardy.

00:24:36.450 --> 00:24:39.290
But then, it never would have evolved as it did in the first place.

00:24:39.610 --> 00:24:42.400
And you and I, we wouldn't even be here.

00:24:43.390 --> 00:24:46.710
Microbes are the very fabric into which all other life is interwoven.

00:24:47.560 --> 00:24:50.520
And not only can environments influence the nature of microbes,

00:24:50.740 --> 00:24:56.120
but as we'll learn in our next episode, microbes can influence the nature of their environments.

